<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>He washed the bleeding sin-wounds,</l><l>And poured in oil and wine;</l><l>He whispered to assure me,</l><l>“I’ve found thee, thou art Mine:”</l><l>I never heard a sweeter voice,</l><l>It made my aching heart rejoice.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>He pointed to the nail-prints,</l><l>For me His blood was shed;</l><l>A mocking crown so thorny,</l><l>Was placed upon His head:</l><l>I wondered what He saw in me,</l><l>To suffer such deep agony.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>I’m sitting in His presence,</l><l>The sunshine of His face,</l><l>While with adoring wonder</l><l>His blessings I retrace.</l><l>It seems as if eternal days</l><l>Are far too short to sound His praise.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>So while the hours are passing,</l><l>All now is perfect rest;</l><l>I’m waiting for the morning,</l><l>The brightest and the best,</l><l>When He will call us to His side,</l><l>To be with Him, His spotless Bride.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
